index 32b4afb5ddf020230f8f0b0839f2545ff1ec9861..a329e4565e2e89e970173242e8aaec3ce91048e1 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -9,8 +9,8 @@
 It contains:
 
 - FreeCAD models and ready-to-3D-print `.3mf` files for a solenoid-based non-destructive physical finger to reset the board and put it into flash mode without having to press the buttons yourself, plus a case for the required USB relay board
-- CLIs and daemons to programmatically:
-  - Trigger the solenoids with via a USB relay board with, with inbuilt rate limits for the relays to prevent them from overheating the solenoids
+- MCP servers to programmatically:
+  - Trigger the solenoids with via a [generic "dcttech.com USBRelay" relay board](https://opentracelab.github.io/website/hardware/multiplexer/dcttech-usbrelay/) with inbuilt rate limits for the relays to prevent them from overheating the solenoids
   - Capture video output and provide emulated mouse/keyboard input via a [NanoKVM-USB](https://github.com/sipeed/NanoKVM-USB)
   - Get early logs/a serial console from the board via UART, and to debug it via JTAG
 - A clean Go reimplementation of the SpacemiT [Titanflasher/flashserver](https://www.spacemit.com/community/document/info?lang=en&nodepath=tools/user_guide/flasher_user_guide.md) to flash U-Boot, EDK2, or an entire OS onto the board
@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@
 ```shell
 $ git clone https://codeberg.org/pojntfx/pushrod
 $ cd pushrod
-$ xdg-open .
+$ go run -exec sudo . # We need root to access the raw USB devices
 ```
 
